The acceptance test (spec.cy.js) is not in this repository - it's external. That's as expected per the user's message.

Now I have a clear understanding of the problem. The toggle checkbox handler in `js/app.js` calls `render()` which replaces `todoList.innerHTML` entirely. This detaches all the `<li>` elements from the DOM, causing Cypress to lose its reference.

The fix is to replace the `render()` call in the toggle handler with surgical DOM updates, just like the toggle-all handler already does.

Let me also check if `finishEdit` and `cancelEdit` have the same problem, since they also call `render()`. But the acceptance test specifically reports about marking/unmarking items as complete, so the toggle is the immediate target.

Actually, wait. Let me re-read the CAPTAIN.md more carefully:

> Fix applied to `js/app.js`: Cypress acceptance suite reported 4 DOM-detachment failures when toggling/clearing/completing todos.
> Root cause: `render()` replaced `todoList.innerHTML` wholesale, destroying all `<li>` elements and detaching Cypress DOM references.
> Fix: surgical DOM updates in the toggle, toggle-all, destroy, and clear-completed event handlers

It says the fix was supposed to have been applied to *toggle* already. But looking at the code, the toggle handler STILL calls `render()`. So the fix wasn't properly applied to the toggle handler! This is the remaining defect.

The CAPTAIN.md also says:
> Pre-existing failures went from 5 to 2 (3 fixed incidentally by surgical DOM updates).

So the toggle handler wasn't fixed yet (still uses `render()`) and that's why those 2 failures remain.

Let me fix it now. I need to replace the `render()` call in the toggle handler with surgical DOM updates similar to what's done for toggle-all.

Here's the toggle handler code:

```javascript
if (target.classList.contains('toggle')) {
  var todos = loadTodos();
  var todo = todos.find(function (t) { return t.id === id; });
  if (todo) {
    todo.completed = !todo.completed;
    saveTodos(todos);
    render();
  }
  return;
}
```

The surgical fix:
```javascript
if (target.classList.contains('toggle')) {
  var todos = loadTodos();
  var todo = todos.find(function (t) { return t.id === id; });
  if (todo) {
    todo.completed = !todo.completed;
    saveTodos(todos);
    // Surgical DOM update: update the specific <li> instead of full re-render
    li.classList.toggle('completed', todo.completed);
    target.checked = todo.completed;
    updateTodoCount(todos);
    updateClearCompleted(todos);
    updateToggleAll(todos);
  }
  return;
}
```

This avoids calling `render()` which replaces `todoList.innerHTML`, so the `<li>` element the Cypress test has a reference to stays attached to the DOM.

Now let me also check the `finishEdit` and `cancelEdit` functions. They also call `render()` - but the acceptance test failure is for marking/unmarking as complete specifically. Let me focus on the toggle for now.

Actually, let me also think about what happens with `finishEdit` and the `focusout` handler. They also call `render()`, but since the acceptance test doesn't fail there, I won't touch them now. The "simplest sufficient change" principle says fix only the failing target.

Let me make the edit.

